    "note": "testdata/4fgl-rows.fit is seven rows of the real 4FGL-DR4 file gll_psc_v35.fit, copied by testdata/mkfermi with their real values. The last four are for Unassociated and are listed under unassociated below. The Galactic Centre source is a point source with an ellipse: its 95% semi-axes are 0.0103 deg, which is 37.08 arcsec, and its position angle is -38.86 deg in the FITS row, which the reader wraps into [0, 360) as 321.14 deg. Its flags are 512, so it is doubtful. The other two have no ellipse in 4FGL: the Small Magellanic Cloud is extended, and a nova has its position fixed from outside. rel is picked: the file holds float32, which is good to about a part in ten million.",
